- Input shape: [N, C, H, W] (or any shape with at least 2 dims)
- num_groups must divide C evenly
- Each group has C/num_groups channels
- For each (n, g), the group spans channels [g*(C/num_groups) : 
(g+1)*(C/num_groups)] and all spatial dimensions
- The normalization is done per-group, per-sample
- Weight and bias are per-channel (shape [C])
- Supports fp16, bf16, fp32

