Thought:
The error is "ub overflow" - the BLOCK_SIZE is too large. The UB (Unified 
Buffer) overflow requires 7340288 bits while only 1572864 bits are available. 
This means I need to use a smaller BLOCK_SIZE and add an inner loop to process 
the data in chunks.

The issue is that for large group sizes (e.g., 2048 channels × 224 × 224 
spatial), the BLOCK_SIZE becomes very large. I need to use a two-level loop:
- Outer loop: grid dimension (one program per group)
- Inner loop: process data in smaller chunks

Let me redesign the kernel to use an inner loop with a smaller BLOCK_SIZE.
