to roughly 192K elements for fp32 accumulators. I need to process the group in 
multiple iterations rather than trying to fit everything into a single block.

The solution is to use a two-pass approach: first accumulate the sum and sum of 
squares across chunks, then compute the mean and variance from those totals. 
This way, each iteration only needs to handle a small block of data, keeping the
accumulator size manageable.

In the second pass, I normalize each element using the precomputed mean and 
variance, then apply the weight and bias before storing the result. The channel 
index is calculated by dividing the offset within the group by the spatial size 
and adding the group offset.

